            {
              "feedback": {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "Incorrect. Entropy can be described as a measure of the dispersal of matter, distribution of kinetic states (microstates), or disorder of a system. Matter that is least dispersed, has the lowest distribution of microstates, and is most ordered (least disordered) has the least entropy. Matter that is most dispersed, has the highest distribution of microstates, and is most disordered has the greatest entropy. Determine whether the process of allowing a gas to expand its volume increases entropy (Δ"
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "S"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": ">0) or decreases entropy (Δ"
